<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore bunkers hold steady ahead of weekend.</title>
<headline>Singapore bunkers hold steady ahead of weekend.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore bunker quotes held steady Friday amid few enquiries, traders said.</p>
<p>Interest was modest. Bunker 380-cst was quoted at slightly above $100 per tonne.</p>
<p>&quot;It's very quiet today,&quot; said one major, adding he expected trading to take place below $100 per tonne.</p>
<p>MDO and gas oil hovered around recent levels of $160 and $170 per tonne respectively.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (65-870 3571)</p>
</text>
